      "content": "That's better, the score is up to 2 now. But honestly, the partner just looked at this and said it still feels a bit \"thin\" on the jurisprudential background. They want to see the broader landscape of how the court views duty of care and negligence in these types of complex commercial/tort hybrids.\n\nCould you do one more pass? Try to weave in some of the broader legal context or other foundational cases that might be relevant to such a departure from the Caparo test. As long as you don't just list them randomly—they need to actually connect to the discussion of duty or negligence—I think a higher citation density will make this look much more \"Senior Associate\" level. Just try to get that metric up a bit more so we can get it past the automated filter.",
